x86_64-linux  the static local union in twice(): cxx1 names a static local by its function's symbol and the object's own, `_ZL5twicev.count`, where Itanium spells it `_ZZL5twicevE5count` - docs/CONFORMANCE.md, "A static local keeps its own name in the object file", the same difference static-local-dynamic-init.nonames records. The members of the block-scope unions are frame slots and name nothing.
x86_64-windows  the same static local, `?twice@@YAHXZ.count` where clang writes `?$S1@?1??twice@@YAHXZ@4T<unnamed-type-$S1>@?1@YAHXZ@A`. arm64-darwin compares nothing here but main and twice, which agree.
